// CotSC localization Batch 23: QBTMEM
@1 = ~...~
@2 = ~...~
@3 = ~...~
@4 = ~...~
@5 = ~Harpers! Dammit! Geherant! Weren't you supposed to guard the entrance?~
@6 = ~We tried, but there were too many! We wouldn't stand a chance!~
@7 = ~No matter. The ritual must go on!~
@8 = ~Cease your babbling, and give up the children, or else you will be harmed. End this wickedness while we give you a chance to surrender!~
@9 = ~Surrender? Bah. I know no such thing. All I know is victory. These children will bring Bhaal back into our world. He will grant us eternal life and exalted status for our oblation.~
@10 = ~You will taste no victory, witch. If that is your will, so be it.~
@11 = ~Enough prattle! Finish them!~
@12 = ~Gorion... this memory... it isn't mine. I don't remember such an event.~
@13 = ~Gorion... this memory... it isn't mine. I don't remember such an event.~
@14 = ~Gorion... this memory... it isn't mine. I don't remember such an event.~
@15 = ~Gorion... this memory... it isn't mine. I don't remember such an event.~
@16 = ~Gorion looks much younger. This happened before he and I were introduced to one another. It makes no sense that you can see it... unless... this isn't your memory.~
@17 = ~But how could that be?~
@18 = ~Perhaps the shard's energy can show you the memories of people who played an important part in your life. Gorion was a father and mentor to you. Perhaps his memories somehow carried over.~
@19 = ~Jan? Do you think that is plausible?~
@20 = ~I suppose it is plausible. The shard's vital energy is beyond my understanding, so I cannot say for certain. It may connect with the recipient's family or friends, or anyone particularly close to them. But that's an educated guess, not an established theory.~
@21 = ~That symbol over there...~
@22 = ~What is it, Imoen?~
@23 = ~The placement of Bhaal's insignia, the altar, Gorion... I know why I recognised this place. I've never seen it in person, but it matches the descriptions. Irenicus... when he experimented on me, I experienced visions. I couldn't understand what they showed. The more he tested my endurance, the more often those fleeting glimpses came to me.~
@24 = ~The shard's power may be reacting to Bhaal's essence in your veins. This temple must still be steeped in the dead god's influence. Perhaps Gorion's memories have become entwined with yours. Imoen may have witnessed a similar connection. You are both children of Bhaal; such a place might draw forth visions you could never otherwise have known.~
@25 = ~That symbol over there...~
@26 = ~What is it, Imoen?~
@27 = ~The placement of Bhaal's insignia, the altar, Gorion... I know why I recognised this place. I've never seen it in person, but it matches the descriptions. Irenicus... when he experimented on me, I experienced visions. I couldn't understand what they showed. The more he tested my endurance, the more often those fleeting glimpses came to me.~
@28 = ~The shard's power may be reacting to Bhaal's essence in your veins. This temple must still be steeped in the dead god's influence. Perhaps Gorion's memories have become entwined with yours. Imoen may have witnessed a similar connection. You are both children of Bhaal; such a place might draw forth visions you could never otherwise have known.~
@29 = ~Harpers! To me!~
@30 = ~Mistress Alianna? Shall I dispose of this garbage, or do we proceed with the ritual?~
@31 = ~Save the ritual for later! Kill them!~
@32 = ~Boys! Run!~
